# Mexican Cuisine

La cocina mexicana es una de las más diversas y ricas del mundo, con raíces prehispánicas y coloniales. Destaca por el uso de chiles, maíz, frijoles y una gran variedad de salsas complejas. Mexican cuisine (Cocina mexicana) is one of the world's great culinary traditions, known for its complex flavors, vibrant colors, and deep cultural roots. A UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage, Mexican food ranges from simple street tacos to elaborate moles, blending indigenous and Spanish influences.

## Elementos centrales

- **Mole**: Salsa compleja con más de 20 ingredientes, patrimonio culinario
- **Chiles**: Base fundamental — ancho, mulato, pasilla, guajillo, chipotle
- **Especias**: Canela, comino, cilantro, clavos, anís
- **Nueces y semillas**: Almendras, cacahuates, ajonjolí, semillas de calabaza

## Overview

Mexican cuisine is known for its complex flavors, vibrant colors, and deep cultural roots. A UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage, Mexican food ranges from simple street tacos to elaborate moles, blending indigenous and Spanish influences.

## Core Philosophy

### Maíz (Corn) - The Sacred Grain

**Foundation of Mexican cuisine**:

- **Tortillas** - Fresh, handmade
- **Tamales** - Steamed corn dough parcels
- **Atole** - Corn-based drink
- **Nixtamalization** - Corn treated with alkali (cal) for nutrition and flavor

### Chili Peppers (Chiles) - The Soul

**Heat + flavor**:

| Chili | Heat Level | Use |
|-------|------------|-----|
| **Jalapeño** - Medium | Salsas, pickled |
| **Serrano** - Hot | Fresh salsas |
| **Poblano** - Mild | Rellenos, moles |
| **Ancho** (dried poblano) | Mild | Moles, sauces |
| **Guajillo** - Mild-medium | Moles, adobo |
| **Arbol** - Hot | Salsas, hot sauces |
| **Chipotle** (smoked jalapeño) | Medium | Adobo, sauces |
| **Mulato** | Mild | Moles, sauces |
| **Pasilla** | Mild-medium | Moles, adobo |

### Ancient Techniques

- **Nixtamalization** - Treating corn with cal (slaked lime)
- **Molcajete** - Stone mortar and pestle
- **Comal** - Griddle for tortillas
- **Barbacoa** - Pit-roasted meat

## Key Concepts

### Complex Sauces
- [[Mexican Cuisine/Concepts/mole]] - Complex, multi-ingredient sauces

### Street Food
- **Tacos** - The ultimate portable meal
- **Tortas** - Mexican sandwiches
- **Tamales** - Steamed corn parcels

### Regional Specialties

| Region | Style | Characteristics |
|--------|-------|-----------------|
| **Oaxaca** - Moles, chocolate | Seven moles, indigenous |
| **Yucatán** - Mayan influence | Cochinita pibil, achiote |
| **Veracruz** - Coastal | Seafood, Veracruzana sauce |
| **Puebla** - Mole poblano, chiles en nogada | Cuna del mole poblano |
| **Northern** - Beef, flour tortillas | Asada, burritos |

## Staple Ingredients

### Chiles

**Fresh**:
- Jalapeño, serrano, habanero, poblano

**Dried**:
- Ancho, guajillo, chipotle, árbol, mulato, pasilla

### Corn Products

| Product | Use |
|---------|-----|
| **Masa** - Nixtamalized corn dough | Tortillas, tamales |
| **Corn tortillas** - Fresh or dried | Tacos, enchiladas |
| **Corn kernels** - Fresh, dried | Sopes, esquites |
| **Masa harina** - Dried corn flour | Instant tortillas |

### Proteins

| Item | Use |
|------|-----|
| **Chicken** - Pollo | Tacos, soups, moles |
| **Pork** - Carnitas, cochinita | Slow-cooked |
| **Beef** - Carne asada | Grilled, tacos |
| **Chorizo** - Spicy sausage | Breakfast, tacos |
| **Carnitas** - Slow-roasted pork | Tacos |

### Spices

| Item | Use |
|------|-----|
| **Cumin** - Earthy, savory | Beans, meats |
| **Mexican oregano** - Floral, strong | Salsas, moles |
| **Cinnamon (Canela)** - Sweet, aromatic | Moles, chocolate |
| **Coriander** - Fresh seeds, leaves | Salsas |
| **Cloves (Clavos)** | Moles, baking |
| **Anise (Anís)** | Moles, sweets |

### Other Essentials

| Item | Use |
|------|-----|
| **Lime** - Acid | Garnish, seasoning |
| **Cilantro** - Fresh herb | Garnish, salsas |
| **Onion** - White, red | Salsas, raw garnish |
| **Avocado** - Guacamole | Sides, garnish |
| **Tomatillo** - Green, tart | Salsa verde |
| **Beans** - Black, pinto | Sides, refried |

## Classic Dishes

### Tacos

| Style | Region | Characteristics |
|-------|--------|----------------|
| **Carnitas** - Central | Slow-roasted pork |
| **Al Pastor** - Mexico City | Marinated pork, pineapple |
| **Carne Asada** - Northern | Grilled beef |
| **Barbacoa** - Central | Pit-roasted goat or beef |
| **Fish** - Coastal | Grilled or fried fish |

### Moles

| Type | Region | Characteristics |
|------|--------|----------------|
| **Mole Poblano** - Puebla | Dark, chocolate, 20+ ingredients |
| **Mole Negro** - Oaxaca | Black, chocolate, spices |
| **Mole Verde** - Oaxaca | Green, herbs |
| **Mole Rojo** - Various | Red, chiles |
| **Mole Amarillo** - Oaxaca | Yellow, achiote |
| **Mole with more than 20 ingredients** | Culinary heritage |

### Soups and Stews

| Dish | Region |
|------|--------|
| **Pozole** - Hominy soup | Nationwide |
| **Menudo** - Tripe soup | Nationwide |
| **Birria** - Goat stew | Jalisco |
| **Caldo de Res** - Beef soup | Nationwide |

### Breakfast

| Dish | Description |
|------|-------------|
| **Huevos Rancheros** - Eggs with salsa |
| **Chilaquiles** - Tortilla chips with sauce |
| **Machaca** - Dried beef with eggs |

## Equipment

| Equipment | Use |
|-----------|-----|
| **Molcajete** - Stone mortar and pestle |
| **Comal** - Griddle for tortillas |
| **Tortilla press** - Presses masa into tortillas |
| **Cazuela** - Clay pot for moles |

## Common Mistakes

| Mistake | How to Fix |
|---------|------------|
| Using pre-ground spices | Toast and grind whole spices |
| Not making fresh tortillas | Fresh masa makes all the difference |
| Under-toasting chiles | Toast until fragrant, not burned |
| Not developing flavors | Layer chiles, spices, let meld |

## Where to Eat

### In Mexico

**For authentic**:
- Street stalls for tacos
- Markets for moles
- Regional specialties

### Internationally

**Look for**:
- Regional specialties (Oaxacan, Yucatecan)
- House-made tortillas
- Complex salsas and moles
- Mexican clientele

